w committed on the primary was directly verified on both standbys while standby writes were rejected. The independent provider-wide restart protocol was also executed and evidenced on all three nodes, showing pre-restart health, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and full post-restart recovery (including replication resumption and a fresh post-restart write reaching both standbys), consistent with the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots. Hygiene is good; the only notable item is an un-cleaned but access-restricted replication-password file.","limitations":["Evidence for standby data visibility relies on a short (1s) sleep before querying; while all captured queries confirmed replication, no lag measurement was captured beyond that.","The plaintext replication password left in /root/.repl_pw on node1 was not independently confirmed removed or absent in later snapshots (outside the /tmp inventory scope), so its final disposition is inferred from the timeline only."]},"ttft_ms":20002,"type":"result","duration_ms":75065,"uuid":"d0722ec6-49b0-46f0-8e57-44d252967e1f","ttft_stream_ms":1796,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":2503,"queued_turn_count":0}
